## Display-device ration

Per page: **one masthead device + one section-label device**, chosen once
and reused. Uppercase-tracked microlabels, sub-12px sizes (max two),
letter-spacing variants — each is a device; devices repeated everywhere
flatten emphasis into texture.

## Hard bans (run assets/bans.sh)

These encode scars (see TASTE.md), not preferences: raw palette classes,
urgency animations, hardcoded hex in app code, saturated display fonts.
Your component library (shadcn/ui etc.) is exempt — it is token-driven and
generator-managed.

## Behavioral floor

Visual work never trades away: visible state (landmarks stay put), labels
with icons for multi-state controls, verbs on buttons (never bare
Yes/No/OK), disabled-not-hidden commands, honest feedback in the user's
vocabulary, reversibility over confirmation. When a redesign is proposed,
run the `taste` verdict protocol: protected functions first, count what
changes, judge behavior before surfaces.
